`ToolInvocation` always records non-string arguments and results as JSON strings and converts objects that are not JSON-serializable through `object_to_any_value`; previously primitives were recorded as-is and other objects through `str()`, e.g. `arguments = 42` was recorded as `42`, now `"42"`. Prompt variables set to `None` are no longer recorded; previously they were recorded as `"null"`.
